<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bandung</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bandung is a city in the highlands of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/java">Java</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indonesia">Indonesia</a>, and the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-java">West Java</a> province. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> rule it grew into a cool hill town with planned Art Deco districts and a technical college, and was intended as a future colonial capital. In January 1950 it was the scene of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raymond-westerling">Raymond Westerling</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-popular-revolutionary-alliance">APRA</a> coup attempt, and in April 1955 it hosted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bandung-conference">Asian–African Conference</a>, a forerunner of the Non-Aligned Movement.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bandung.jpg" alt="Bandung" width="320" height="178" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: F1fans · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bandung_View_dari_Gedung_Wisma_HSBC_Asia_Afrika_4.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
